# Each maker runs once and its scope holds a text, which the collector could let go with the scope. The closure that keptForGood returns on every way goes, by the one call, into a variable of the module that
# never holds anything else: closure and scope live as long as the program, so the scope is never made and its names are words of the instance. The others keep their scopes: the variable is stored again;
# the closure is dropped at once; one of two closures comes back; the answer goes to a call first; the call stands under a handler. f1 = keptForGood .. f6 = underTry
